        "id": 9075,
        "name": "Tipx",
        "username": "Tipx",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ebca7d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-28T21:01:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I tried searching the forum to understand how&nbsp;<span>Wrest the Mind&nbsp;</span><span>behaves when a target deals damage to multiple targets. For the purpose of this exercice, let's say \"BOB\" (a fictive card) has the card&nbsp;</span><span>Wrest the Mind</span><span>&nbsp;played on him, in a 4 player game. BOB has the ability \"On [Whatever], deal all hero caracters 2 fire damage\". [Whatever] happens. So the posibilities I see:</span></p><p><span>1- Visionary activates the ability and is able to redirect 8 (2 + 2 + 2 + 2) fire damage on a single target, then deals 3 damages to both her and the target. (The order is not an issue, it has been stated multiple times in some rulings.)</span></p><p><span>2- Visionary activates the ability and is able to redirect 2 fire damage on a single target,&nbsp;</span><span>then deals 3 damages to both her and the target. Visionary can then do it up to 3 other times (one for each other hero.)</span></p><p><span>3- Visionary activates the ability and is able to redirect 2 fire damage</span><span>&nbsp;on a single target, then can activates the abilities up to 3 other times&nbsp;</span><span>(one for each other hero), then&nbsp;</span><span>then deals 3 damages to both her and the target up to 4 times.</span></p><p>I think 3 is clearly not what's happening, but I would understand whether it's 1 or 2. Any thoughts?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:46.433Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
