        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I tried searching the forum to understand how&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(68, 68, 68); font-family: 'PT Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">Wrest the Mind&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">behaves when a target deals damage to multiple targets. For the purpose of this exercice, let&#39;s say &quot;BOB&quot; (a fictive card) has the card&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(68, 68, 68); font-family: 'PT Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">Wrest the Mind</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;played on him, in a 4 player game. BOB has the ability &quot;On [Whatever], deal all hero caracters 2 fire damage&quot;. [Whatever] happens. So the posibilities I see:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">1- Visionary activates the ability and is able to redirect 8 (2 + 2 + 2 + 2) fire damage on a single target, then deals 3 damages to both her and the target. (The order is not an issue, it has been stated multiple times in some rulings.)</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">2- Visionary activates the ability and is able to redirect 2 fire damage on a single target,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">then deals 3 damages to both her and the target. Visionary can then do it up to 3 other times (one for each other hero.)</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">3- Visionary activates the ability and is able to redirect 2 fire damage</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;on a single target, then can activates the abilities up to 3 other times&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(one for each other hero), then&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">then deals 3 damages to both her and the target up to 4 times.</span></p><p>I think 3 is clearly not what&#39;s happening, but I would understand whether it&#39;s 1 or 2. Any thoughts?</p>",
