        "raw": "I would say it&#39;s the second one. Wrest activates [i]whenever[/i] its target deals damage. If Bob is hitting four different targets (with his multi-hit ability), that is four separate instances of damage and so each one can trigger Wrest, permitting Visionary to redirect all four instances of damage as they occur (and then dealing Bob and herself three points of psychic damage) before moving onto the next instance of damage. Obviously if the psychic feedback effect kills Bob after he&#39;s had his first couple of damage instances redirected (should Visionary choose to do so), the whole thing stops, Bob is destroyed and thus so is Wrest (and Visionary doesn&#39;t hit herself after that point because the card telling her to do so has just been destroyed before she got to that bit on that particular attack).\n",
