        "id": 83021,
        "name": "Medic-Tank",
        "username": "Medic-Tank",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-28T22:37:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"grysqrl\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/48/1909_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> grysqrl:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Option 2 is correct. For each instance of damage dealt, you can choose to activate Wrest the Mind (redirect the damage, damage the WtM target, damage Visionary). It should be noted that if the second step (damaging the target that WtM is played on) kills the target, Wrest the Mind is also destroyed and deals no damage to Visionary.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thus if we replace Bob with Citizen Hammer 3 Hp and 3 fire damage to all hero targets you would only redirect the first instance before he died, whil Citizen Winter with 4 Hp could withstand the first 3 damage and succomb to the second redirection if not already damaged.&nbsp;</p>",
